-- the headline number the task quotes --
  limit=8192, pad=0    : 61 tok, 0.016 s
  limit=8192, pad=6000 : 5946 tok, 3.505 s
  MEASURED raw ratio   = 219.06x  for a 97.48x input growth
  MODELLED ratio for the same two input lengths = 607.471x  -> measured/modelled = 0.361 (model OVER-predicts by 2.77x)
  The FLOP model has NO constant term, so it cannot describe the 61-token endpoint:
    modelled latency growth n=61 -> n=5946 (pure FLOPs) = 97.5x,
    measured growth at the same two points           = 219.1x,
    so the model OVER-predicts by 2.77x (anything < 1 means measured < modelled).
    n=61 -> n=1032: modelled 31.5x vs measured 13.2x - the model OVER-predicts the small-n end by 2.39x.
    Conversely at n=5946 -> 6912 the model UNDER-predicts by 0.97x. No single FLOPs-only model
    fits both ends: it needs a constant term at small n and a super-quadratic term at large n.

