   m= 10 comparisons: P(>=1 false positive | all null) = 0.401; Bonferroni alpha = 0.00500
   m= 25 comparisons: P(>=1 false positive | all null) = 0.723; Bonferroni alpha = 0.00200
   m= 50 comparisons: P(>=1 false positive | all null) = 0.923; Bonferroni alpha = 0.00100

Bonferroni-corrected alpha needs a larger raw p; per-cell n to keep the SAME MDE
under alpha=0.05/m scales as n * (z_(1-a/2m)/z_(1-a/2))^2 (zq defined above):
   m=  1: z=1.9600, inflation factor vs m=1 = 1.000
   m= 10: z=2.8070, inflation factor vs m=1 = 2.051
   m= 25: z=3.0902, inflation factor vs m=1 = 2.486
   m= 50: z=3.2905, inflation factor vs m=1 = 2.819

resolution floor: with n items and a 4-option task, accuracy is a multiple of 1/n.
   n=  20: one item = 0.0500 accuracy; floor resolution with a majority-class baseline of 0.35 is 7/20
   n= 200: one item = 0.0050 accuracy; floor resolution with a majority-class baseline of 0.35 is 70/200
   n= 400: one item = 0.0025 accuracy; floor resolution with a majority-class baseline of 0.35 is 140/400
   n= 600: one item = 0.0017 accuracy; floor resolution with a majority-class baseline of 0.35 is 210/600

==============================================================================
6. HEAD-BLOCK WIDTH PROBE (fork source, CPU tokenizer only)
==============================================================================
Builds the real sequence with the shipped tokenizer and the real upstream question,
so the marker positions and the state start are COMPUTED, not assumed.

  question: upstream department (4 long options)
    max_len= 1024 head_max_len=256: len(ids)=1024 markers=[12, 22] -> last marker m*=22, state block starts at 23+len(last option), HEAD WIDTH for the marker = 23 tokens
    max_len= 8192 head_max_len=256: len(ids)=8192 markers=[12, 22] -> last marker m*=22, state block starts at 23+len(last option), HEAD WIDTH for the marker = 23 tokens
    max_len= 8192 head_max_len=192: len(ids)=8192 markers=[12, 22] -> last marker m*=22, state block starts at 23+len(last option), HEAD WIDTH for the marker = 23 tokens
    max_len=  512 head_max_len=192: len(ids)= 512 markers=[12, 22] -> last marker m*=22, state block starts at 23+len(last option), HEAD WIDTH for the marker = 23 tokens

  question: short 2-option yes/no
    max_len= 1024 head_max_len=256: len(ids)=1024 markers=[10, 20] -> last marker m*=20, state block starts at 21+len(last option), HEAD WIDTH for the marker = 21 tokens
    max_len= 8192 head_max_len=256: len(ids)=8192 markers=[10, 20] -> last marker m*=20, state block starts at 21+len(last option), HEAD WIDTH for the marker = 21 tokens
    max_len= 8192 head_max_len=192: len(ids)=8192 markers=[10, 20] -> last marker m*=20, state block starts at 21+len(last option), HEAD WIDTH for the marker = 21 tokens
    max_len=  512 head_max_len=192: len(ids)= 512 markers=[10, 20] -> last marker m*=20, state block starts at 21+len(last option), HEAD WIDTH for the marker = 21 tokens

  The marker's position m* is the parameter that matters for reachability, and it
  is set by head_max_len and the option rendering; the state block sits AFTER it.
